# Each distinct call is a constraint-valid input; expected values are generated by the golden solution.
VALIDITY = "Argument values follow these problem constraints:\n- 2 <= n <= 10^4\n- encoded.length == n - 1\n- 0 <= encoded[i] <= 10^5\n- 0 <= first <= 10^5\n\nSemantic and boundary checks: Inputs meet the statement bounds and use valid argument shapes; exact minimum/maximum scalar values and maximum practical input sizes are included where practical. Every legal statement example input is included in CASES."

